//
// xTCP - treatment journal
//
// The host-side intent journal of the route treatment agent: the desired
// state last accepted from the controller, the local hold, and one record per
// assignment with the exact kernel route bytes that were installed. It is a
// FILE FORMAT, read and written only on the host by the agent, the watchdog
// and the local treatmentctl commands, and never an RPC payload.
//
// It is a separate proto package from xtcp_treatment.v1 on purpose: the host
// side (pkg/treatment/reconcile, the watchdog) must be able to read and write
// the journal without linking the gRPC service stubs that share a Go package
// with the RPC messages. The messages below therefore repeat the treatment
// shape rather than importing it; pkg/treatment/reconcile converts them to
// and from the domain types, and the domain validators run on every load.
//
// Values of the two enums mirror xtcp_treatment.v1 one-for-one and the domain
// enums in pkg/treatment; reconcile's tests pin the correspondence.
//
// See docs/tcp-controller.md, "Persistence, restart and withdrawal".

